{
  "edgesLine": "19 must sit next to 18, on its diagonal. Only this square does, so it must be 19.",
  "edgesLines": "2 must be on its row, within a step of 1's column and 3's column. Only this square is, so it must be 2.",
  "edgesPointers": "Of the missing numbers, only 1, 3 and 23 point here. 3 is too far from 4's column and 23 from 22's row, so it must be 1.",
  "fill": "No other run can reach this square, and 3 steps from 13 rules out anything higher, so it must be 10.",
  "hexagonRun": "Only 15, between 14 and 16, can reach this square, so it must be 15.",
  "rectBetween": "14 must sit next to both 13 and 15, and this is the only empty square that does, so it must be 14.",
  "rectRun": "Only 23, between 22 and 24, can reach this square, so it must be 23.",
  "wholeRun": "The run between 3 and 6 has only one route through the empty squares, so it must go along the line.",
}
`;
